= <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> and <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> Alliance

With new elections approaching, the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> is likely to be pushed into irrelevance by the surging <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>. In an effort to ensure his party's survival, Coalfax has concluded an alliance with Mallin and the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>.

While Coalfax insists that the pact is purely technical and does not compromise the party’s political integrity, it proves to be the final straw for the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>'s left wing. An accommodation with the anti-democratic and "socially reactionary" Mallin is widely seen as a betrayal of the <span style="color: #98C22C;">National Liberal</span> legacy that Stratton and the founders of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> once championed.

- @dvp_left_split

@dvp_left_split
title: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>'s left wing splits!
on-arrival: hugenberg_gold = 1; guild_gold *= 0.8; burgher_gold *= 0.5; faithful_gold *= 0.8; pro_republic -= 3; liberal_cooperation -= 10; bourgeois_cooperation -= 10; gold_right += 25; gold_relation -= 50
face-image: img/dvp_poster_2.jpg

Those on the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>'s left wing who had quietly opposed Coalfax's turn to the right have now resigned en masse. Tarian Beckley, Florian Vellt, and Caspar Holt—prominent figures within the white-collar DHV union—have also stepped down, with Beckley being the longtime chairman of the association.

With their exodus, the party’s last remaining link to the Commonwealth white-collar movement has been severed, along with a significant portion of its electoral base. The only consolation Coalfax can claim is that the party’s loss in seats will be somewhat mitigated by its electoral connection to the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>.